# Make fingerprint survive a /data wipe (factory reset / EDL stock<->LOS swap).
#
# What a /data wipe actually destroys is the virtual-HAL config props (they live in
# /data/property/persistent_properties). Without them the framework never treats the
# sensor as UDFPS, so there is no onPointerDown and enroll goes nowhere. Re-assert them
# in post-fs-data, BEFORE the Goodix HAL starts.
#
# This rc used to ALSO copy a per-unit calibration from /product/etc/goodix_cal into
# /data/vendor/goodix. That was wrong and is removed (2026-08-06):
#   - The real per-unit cal is /mnt/vendor/persist/goodix/cali_data_0.so. /mnt/vendor/persist
#     is factory-programmed, per-device and is NOT wiped by a factory reset, so every phone
#     already has its own. We never flash that partition.
#   - The /data/vendor/goodix/cali_*.so are runtime base images, not calibration. Verified on
#     hardware: with /data/vendor/goodix emptied the HAL still reports cali_state 2, regenerates
#     every one of those files by itself, and enroll + unlock work.
#   - So shipping one phone's files to everyone gave every OTHER user another sensor's base
#     images. That is why FP only ever worked on the build machine's phone.
# See memory nx809j_fp_persist_partition_cal.
#
# (init-domain writes to vendor data + sets vendor props — relies on the device shipping
# permissive; see BoardConfig.)

on post-fs-data
    # Virtual-HAL config props (persist; re-asserted each boot for the post-wipe case)
    setprop persist.vendor.fingerprint.virtual.type udfps
    setprop persist.vendor.fingerprint.virtual.sensor_location 608:2024:94
    setprop persist.vendor.fingerprint.virtual.udfps.control_illumination true
    setprop persist.vendor.fingerprint.virtual.udfps.display_touch false

    # The HAL creates and owns everything in here; just make sure it exists and is labelled.
    mkdir /data/vendor/goodix 0700 system system
    restorecon_recursive /data/vendor/goodix

    # One-shot migration for phones that already ran an older build: drop the foreign cal
    # those builds copied in, so the HAL regenerates its own. Self-limiting via a marker
    # file; a no-op on clean flashes and on every boot after the first.
    exec_start fp_cal_purge

service fp_cal_purge /system/bin/sh /product/etc/goodix/fp-cal-purge.sh
    user root
    group root system
    disabled
    oneshot
